     "text": "{\"count\": 2, \"rationale\": \"crown:obtain is an OR of three branches, so all three must be cut. Branch 1: h5_0:escalate depends only on the chain h3_1:traverse <- h1_0:reach <- footholds. Blocking any one of h5_0, h3_1 or h1_0 cuts it. Branches 2 and 3: h5_1:reach and h5_2:obtain are both AND steps that require h3_0:traverse. Blocking h3_0 therefore cuts both. Why one block is not enough: none of h5_0, h3_1 or h1_0 lies on the path to h3_0, which comes from h2_0 and h2_2. Likewise, h3_0 is not on the h5_0 chain. So no single step cuts every branch. A minimum set is {h3_0:traverse, h1_0:reach}, which has 2 steps.\"}"
